 "title": "Priced Later Programs - Full Circle Ag",
 "text": "Priced Later Programs - Full Circle Ag\nMain\nUtilities\nAbout\nScholarships\nHistory\nLeadership & Board Members\nDonation Request Form\nCredit Policy\nLocations\nNews\nSeasonal Snapshot\nAgronomy\nAg Tech Summit\nAcres to Insights\nAgronomy Team\nEnergy\nCenex Total Protection Plan\nOut of Gas Policy\nPropane Order Form\nEnergy Team\nFeed\nGrain\nPriced Later Programs\nGrain for Goodness\nCash Bids\nGrain Offers\nGrain Policies\nProducer Financing\nAccount Login\nCareers\nContact Us\nLocations\nAccount Login\nLocations\nContact Us\nCareers\nPriced Later Programs\nBenefits of a Priced Later Contract\nFlexibility for your farm\nYou choose when to price your grain (within the timeline stated in your contract).\nGrain is priced at the posted cash bid at the elevator on the day you set the price.\nPriced Later Contracts\nKey Rules & Restrictions\nBushels on a Priced Later Contract cannot : Be priced off or applied to another contract (e.g., Cash, Futures Fixed, Basis Fixed, Priced).\nBe rewritten into a new or existing contract.\nBe sold using a future point-in-time bid.\nBushels on a Priced Later Contract are delivered bushels and are always priced at the current day’s cash bid , using: The elevator’s current basis , and\nThe current futures month .\nFuture delivery periods cannot be used to price already-delivered bushels.\nPriced Later Service Fee\n$0.07 per bushel per month (applies to all commodities).\nContract Requirements\nPriced Later Contracts must be signed and returned within 30 days of delivery. Per the North Dakota Department of Agriculture , this ensures you maintain ownership of your bushels.\nAdditional Notes\nBushels on a Priced Later Contract are not eligible to be applied to a future delivery contract.\nContracts may be priced during normal marketing hours at the posted bid.\nAll DP programs are subject to change or discontinuation at any time.\nRolling Contracts\nFutures Fixed and Basis Fixed contracts may only be rolled within the same marketing year, and are allowed to be rolled the one time .\nA Roll Fee of $0.01 /bushel will be applied to any contract roll.\nContact Us\nWe are happy to work with you to develop a customized risk management plan using any or a variety of alternative contracts available through StoneX. Utilizing our StoneX Consultants and the tools available, we can help you achieve price targets while protecting against unacceptable price risk. This allows you to make the final pricing decisions on your grain throughout the season.\nDon't forget to let our Transportation Department handle your grain hauling! With reliable trucks and drivers, we’ll get your grain to the elevator efficiently. Give us a call today to schedule your grain pick up!\nKali Colbert\nGrain Procurement Specialist\nJustin Ostby\nGrain Division Manager\nTJ Johnson\nTransportation Division Manager\n+ −\nLeaflet | © OpenStreetMap contributors\nHave you downloaded our app yet?\nCompany\nContact Us\nCareers\nLocations\nFull Circle Ag\n520 Vander Horck\nPO Box 148\nBritton SD 57430\nP:605-824-6815\nE:info@fullcircle.com\n@2026 Full Circle Ag. All rights reserved. View data privacy policy\nCompany\nContact Us\nCareers\nLocations\nHome\nFull Circle Ag\n520 Vander Horck Ave\nBritton, SD 57430\n1-605-448-2231\nConnect with Centra Sota\n-->\nSearch for:\nMinimum 3 character allowed.\nKali Colbert\nGrain Procurement Specialist\nOffice: (701) 997-2970\ncolbertk@fullcircleag.com\n×\nJustin Ostby\nGrain Division Manager\nOffice: (701) 997-2970\nostbyj@fullcircleag.com\n×\nTJ Johnson\nTransportation Division Manager\nOffice: (701) 997-2970\njohnsontj@fullcircleag.com\n×",
